meta {
  name: Delete Product Relationship (Safe Unlink)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID/relationships/REPLACE_WITH_RELATIONSHIP_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against the same disposable scratch products
  and relationship type as "Create Product Relationship Link.bru" on
  "David's Dev Account".

  ## Major, genuinely good finding -- the first confirmed SAFE scoped
  unlink in this entire project
  Every prior "remove one related thing from a product" mechanism tested
  in this project has been actively dangerous: `DELETE
  /products/{id}/categories` (2-segment subpath) deletes the **entire
  product**, not just the category link (quirk #31); the newly-documented
  "1:M Unlink" pattern `DELETE /products/{id}/categories/{category_id}`
  (3-segment) does the exact same thing (quirk #54). Both are open
  questions #12/#20 in `config/api-testing.config.md` -- "is there any
  safe DELETE-based unlink at all?"

  **This new endpoint is the answer, at least for relationships**:
  `DELETE /products/{product_id}/relationships/{relationship_id}` --
  confirmed `204`, and a follow-up `GET /products/{product_id}` shows the
  product **fully intact** (`sku`, `label`, `status` all unchanged) with
  only `product_relationships` now emptied to `[]`. This is a real,
  properly-scoped removal -- the first one found in the whole API. Worth
  highlighting prominently in any how-to docs about removing a product
  relationship, and worth re-raising with Plytix alongside open question
  #20: *why* does this new dedicated endpoint get scoped deletion right
  when the older subpath-based patterns don't?

  Note the URL shape: this only removes the *entire relationship-type
  link* (all related products under that `relationship_id` for this
  product), not one individual related product out of a multi-product
  link -- removing a single related product from a link with several
  requires `PATCH`ing a reduced `related_products` array instead (not
  separately tested this session, but consistent with every other
  "safe removal via PATCH" pattern found in this project).
}

example {
  name: Delete Product Relationship - Success (204, Product Stays Intact)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, unlinking the relationship created earlier in this session.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23f/relationships/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23e
    method: delete
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 204
      text: No Content
    }
    headers: {
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        (empty body)
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Get Product by ID - After Delete (Product Intact, Relationship Gone)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, follow-up GET on the PRODUCT (not the relationship) immediately after the DELETE above -- the product is still fully present, unlike every other subpath-delete hazard found in this project.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23f
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23f",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "sku": "WC-TEST-REL-A",
            "label": "WC Test Relationship Product A",
            "status": "Draft",
            "attributes": {},
            "thumbnail_id": null,
            "parent_id": null,
            "num_variations": 0,
            "product_level": 0,
            "product_family_id": null,
            "overwritten_attributes": [],
            "product_relationships": [],
            "created": "2026-09-15T17:06:52.993000",
            "modified": "2026-09-15T17:32:58.807000"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
